            ['question' => 'Can a pitch deck be prepared from an existing draft?', 'answer' => 'Yes. An existing pitch deck can be reviewed and refined, or a new presentation can be prepared using information about the business model, market opportunity, revenue strategy, financial projections, and funding requirements. The content should reflect the startup\'s actual position and the intended audience. Reviewing the company\'s financial position through <a class="internal-link" href="/accounting-and-reporting/financial-statement-analysis">financial statement analysis</a> can also help founders organise relevant financial information for investor discussions.'],
            ['question' => 'What documents are needed for Startup India recognition?', 'answer' => 'The required information generally includes details about the business entity, incorporation or registration documents, and a description of the startup\'s activities and innovation or improvement. Additional details may be requested depending on the application and current requirements. For a broader understanding of company incorporation, document requirements, and registration procedures, read our <a class="internal-link" href="/blog/company-registration-process-step-by-step-guide/">company registration guide</a>.'],
            ['question' => 'Can I get support for the entire funding process or just one service?', 'answer' => 'Both options may be considered depending on your requirements. You can seek assistance with a specific service or coordinate multiple services as part of a broader funding engagement. The scope and deliverables should be agreed before work begins. Founders preparing their business for the next stage of growth should also understand common administrative and filing issues; our guide to <a class="internal-link" href="/blog/mistakes-to-avoid-business-registration-chennai/">mistakes to avoid during business registration</a> offers additional information on this topic.'],
        ];
